MaintainerNotes: |-
  ThothTerm Rolling is an independent app that runs an Arch Linux ARM AArch64
  environment under PRoot. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by the Arch
  Linux or Arch Linux ARM projects. The Arch Linux trademark policy requires
  permission for any mark beginning with "Arch", so the product name is
  neutral; "Arch Linux ARM" appears only as a factual description of the
  guest, and no Arch artwork is used. The package id com.thothterm.arch names
  the guest distribution (docs/branding/arch/TRADEMARK.md).

  arm64-v8a only. minSdk 26, targetSdk 36. A separate app from ThothTerm
  Ubuntu (com.thothterm.ubuntu) and ThothTerm Trixie (com.thothterm.debian);
  all three are built on the same code, which lives in garden-common/.

  The fdroid flavour packages no distribution binaries. The full flavour's
  rootfs staging task runs only for preFull*Build, so this build makes no
  network requests of its own. On first run the app downloads the Arch Linux
  ARM userland only after an explicit opt-in, from the project's GitHub
  release @ROOTFS_TAG@, and refuses it unless its size and SHA-256 match
  garden-arch/src/main/assets/garden/distro.properties (@ROOTFS_SIZE@ bytes,
  sha256 @ROOTFS_SHA@).

  That archive is not an Arch Linux ARM-published file. It is built by
  garden-arch/rootfs/build-rootfs.sh: the official
  ArchLinuxARM-aarch64-latest.tar.gz is verified against the Arch Linux ARM
  Build System key (68B3537F39A313B3E574D06777193F152BDBE6A6) and used only as
  the build environment; pacman installs base + archlinuxarm-keyring sudo
  ca-certificates curl into an empty root from freshly synced repositories,
  each package signature-checked, fully upgraded as of the build. It holds
  unmodified Arch Linux ARM packages only, ships no pacman keyring, sync
  databases, cache or lock, and is reproducible byte for byte from the
  captured, hash-pinned inputs. The corresponding source of every package
  (recipe and upstream sources) is published in the same release. On first
  run the app creates the installation's own pacman keyring (pacman-key
  --init, --populate archlinuxarm) and verifies it offline before setup
  completes, so pacman works immediately with signature checking on.
  Provenance: docs/garden/arch/ROOTFS_PROVENANCE.md.

  The PRoot runtime is compiled during the build by
  garden-common/tools/build-proot.sh from sources in the repository:
  third_party/proot (termux/proot, tag v5.1.107.92) and
  third_party/libandroid-shmem (termux/libandroid-shmem, tag v0.7) as
  submodules, plus talloc 2.4.3's talloc.c and talloc.h vendored verbatim. The
  script verifies both submodule commits, downloads nothing, and checks 16 KB
  page alignment. submodules: true is therefore required. PRoot is GPL-2.0 and
  talloc LGPL-3.0; the corresponding source is the pinned submodules, the five
  patches in garden-common/patches and the build script, all in the tagged
  commit.

  LAN Mode is an HTTP/WebSocket server, off by default, that the user turns on
  to use the terminal from a browser on the same Wi-Fi or Ethernet network
  after pairing with a one-time PIN. It binds only a private LAN address, uses
  no external service, and serves only assets packaged in the APK
  (garden-common/src/main/assets/lan). Its xterm.js bundle is built unminified
  from npm packages pinned by sha512 by garden-common/lan-web/build.mjs;
  `npm ci --ignore-scripts && node build.mjs --check` reproduces the committed
  files. The Gradle build does not run Node. Uploads into the terminal's
  current directory use the Storage Access Framework on the phone (no storage
  permission) and four authenticated endpoints in LAN Mode.

  Release builds are minified with proguard-android-optimize.txt plus
  garden-common/consumer-rules.pro, which holds two keep rules only: the native
  library registers its methods by the literal class names
  com/thothterm/TermIO$Native and com/thothterm/Process$Native.

